<BaseLayout title="DC Motor Transfer Functions — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>DC Motor Transfer Functions</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The first system in this course whose two states feed each other: current
    makes torque, speed makes back-EMF. Both disturbance paths share one
    numerator, <code>D(s)</code>, and its roots are the zeros of the stiffness.
    Move the winding resistance and watch them ride a circle, collide, and
    split — the three cases the lecture annotates are one slider apart.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
